WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We maybe have done ourselves
a disservice

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.872
of adapting to how outrageous

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
and shocking the news is
every day,

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we´ve lost our capacity
to be shocked by it.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:13.546
-You know, the incredible
superpower of human beings

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that they can
make things normal.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.916
Their adaptability, right?

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, what´s the species
that can live

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the Amazon and the Arctic?
-Right.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right? And the reason is,
we´re very good

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
at just being, like,
"Well, it´s cold all the time.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.795
We´re gonna build an igloo, and
we´re gonna hunt some whales,

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.430
and we´re gonna get through."

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so because that is
the human-being superpower --

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is the essence
in some ways of being a human.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.638 size:88% position:44%
You adjust and acclimate

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.340 size:78% position:39%
to whatever situation
you find yourself in.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so the president
goes on Twitter and says,

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.743
"I am, in front of all of you,

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
officially instructing
my attorney general

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
to open an investigation
of my chief political rival."

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, no, you can´t do that.
-Right.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:54.354
-If you did that in secret
and we found out about it,

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:55.789
that might be impeachable.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.857
If Barack Obama did that, it
would probably be impeachable.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
But because
we´re sort of acclimated --

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.694
Like, "Oh, he´s tweeting again."
-Yeah.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, he --
It is amazing in some ways

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
what we are able
to acclimate to.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.069
-Well, the other thing
that´s amazing is it seems like

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
it´s not just people who are
critical of the president

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sort of
on the opposing side,

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:16.076
it seems like people within
the president´s inner circle

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
also say,
"Hey, you can´t listen

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:21.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
to what he says
or writes or does.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:24.584
Like, that´s -- that´s not fair
to take him at his word."

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.587 size:78% position:39%
He´s full of [bleep].

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, don´t you think
that´s what they´re saying?

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes! In fact --
And I actually think my --

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.060
One of my theories about the man
is that in some weird way,

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we think of him
as avaricious

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
and ambitious
and he wants to be powerful.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.766
I think it´s the opposite.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.502
I think what he actually wants
is the trappings of the office,

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.538
but he mostly wants to be a guy
live-tweeting "Fox &amp; Friends."

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.140
I don´t think he actually --

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.642
In a weird way, I don´t think
he wants the responsibility.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.211 size:75% position:38%
Like, he wants to be
the guy at the bar

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.046
that everyone has to listen to.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think he likes
living in the Oval Office.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when it´s like, "Hey, sir,
we´ve got a tough decision

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make here about what
we´re doing in North Korea."

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s like, "I´d rather
live-tweet ´Fox &amp; Friends.´"

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.188 size:78% position:39%
You know what I mean?

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it´s like --
Not only do his defenders say,

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.825
"Well, that´s just him talking,"

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
in an own way,
like, he doesn´t seem to care

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what actually happens
in the world.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.732
What he cares about is that
the attention is on him.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:15.535
-So you think if we just let
him, like, take the Oval Office

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:18.037
and, like, remove it and, like,
roll it to New York...

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.540
-"Truman Show" it.
-And he could just do a podcast.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. If you gave --

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:25.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you gave Donald Trump a
podcast, he would be so happy.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.315 size:84% position:42%
-And the world would be
such a better place.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.318
-I would love it. I would listen
to a Donald Trump podcast.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.687 size:75% position:38%
-Give him a podcast!

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, all right.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.895
Well, I guess we just pitch it
to him and see what happens.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:43.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Sir, we need about
30 minutes of your time.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.031
We´ll be right in and out."

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.000
-Thanks so much for being here.
It´s always a pleasure.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have a great show tonight.
Chris Hayes, everybody!

